{
  "id": "murphy-shakti8-feelgood-1phase-frontal",
  "name": "8 Coil Shakti Feelgood: one phase, frontal",
  "category": "mood",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (8 Coil Shakti); signal templates licensed from Persinger & Koren",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's one-phase Feelgood session: the amygdala and hippocampal signals one after the other with 4-s pauses, over both frontal lobes only. The vendor calls it 'the most effective feelgood session' and says to begin with it rather than the two-phase version.",
  "notes": "Phase 1 (20 min) is the 20-min version (Murphy's demo video: 'choose 20 minutes, that's usually a fine length for most people'): stop after it, or let phase 2 run for the 30-min version. Four coils over the frontal lobes (Fp1, AF3, Fp2, AF4 on CH5-8, the frontal group of the two-phase files; CH1-4 stay silent). The vendor describes this session as 'running the 'feelgood' session, and bypassing the first phase', 'doing only the second phase, which applies the signals only to the frontal lobes'; its 2019 photo of the single-phase setup labels the two right coils R and the two left coils L, and the demo video shows the signal on 'both stereo channels at once', so all four coils carry the same signal at the same time. Polarity as in that photo and the older front view: AF4 (upper right) and Fp1 (lower left) +, AF3 (upper left) and Fp2 (lower right) - (weight -1). The exact sites are an inference from the photos. The vendor's signals are proprietary. One pass here is: the amygdala signal, approximated by the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz, 230 points of 3 ms = 0.69 s; the 230-point length is from Ryczko & Persinger 2002); 4 s of silence (the vendor: 'generated one after the other ... with a four-second latency'); the hippocampal 'LTP' signal, approximated by four theta bursts of 4 pulses at 100 Hz (the Larson & Lynch timing of the project's ltp generator) at the 5.4 Hz spectral peak the vendor reports for it (0.6 s, with 1-ms points instead of the vendor's 3-ms points so the 100 Hz pulses fit); then 4 s of silence again. That gives about 8 s of field per minute (the vendor states 9.6 s). The vendor says you may feel 'a bit foggy' right after, and that too many frontal (or temporal) series can produce 'malaise', so alternate frontal and temporal series. Intensity: the Shakti software defaults to 50% volume, which the vendor calls the 50 mG 'laboratory standard' (5 µT), while its measurement page gives 10 mG (1 µT) as the normal peak; no independent measurement of a Shakti unit was found, and this file uses 1 µT. Persinger's lab reported better mood with weekly burst-firing fields in small samples (Baker-Price & Persinger 1996, 2003, the latter with temporal or left-frontal placement; Tsang et al. 2009); none has been independently replicated. An independent randomized sham-controlled test of the 8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal over the temporal lobes found no effect on emotional responses (Gendle & McGrath 2012; Murphy argues it used the wrong session), and a double-blind God Helmet test found no field effect (Granqvist 2005). The same lab reported more aggression after three weekly bilateral burst-firing sessions (Gillis & Persinger 1993) and more acceptance of false statements with burst-firing over the left prefrontal region (Ross, Koren & Persinger 2008). Not a treatment for depression or any illness: the vendor excludes people with psychiatric diagnoses. Not for people with epilepsy; stop if distressed. Revised after a re-check of the vendor's Feelgood pages (2026): coil polarity added (all four coils had the same polarity before), and the 'not in sensory deprivation' rule, the demo's 20-min suggestion and the vendor's intensity figures noted. Still approximate: the coil sites and both signal templates.",
  "setting": "Not in sensory deprivation: the vendor says the Feelgood session 'should not be done in sensory deprivation', since it is meant for 'outward-looking', 'this-worldly' effects. Evenings, so that any effect is noticed the next morning, as the vendor advises.",
  "schedule": "Vendor: 6 weekly sessions or 6 sessions every 3 days (never more often than every 72 h), then 3 weeks off. If a series is interrupted, wait 3 days and restart.",
  "targets": ["vmpfc", "left-dlpfc", "right-dlpfc"],
